{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And this is the thing that you shall do to them</b> — meaning, draw them near through speech: say to them, אשרי תבחר ותקרב (happy is the one You choose and bring near)." "<b>Take</b> — two times in the Masorah: this one and the other לקח בגדו כי ערב זר. Because Aaron made the calf, HaShem said to remove his defiled garments from him, for the garments of an ע\"א (unclean person) transmit impurity, and this is what is said: לקח בגדו — meaning, from him, כי ערב זר."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:39.255378443Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}